# Findings inside the cloudflared binary itself, which is Cloudflare's build,
# not ours. There is no newer release to move to: 2026.8.3 is the latest, and
# it is compiled with Go 1.26.4 against golang.org/x/crypto v0.53.0.
#
# The alternative is to compile cloudflared ourselves from the tagged source
# with a current toolchain and a bumped x/crypto. That would clear these, and
# it would also mean shipping a cloudflared that Cloudflare did not build, did
# not sign and will not support — for a daemon whose whole job is holding an
# authenticated tunnel into your network. Taking their binary is the more
# defensible of the two, so these are suppressed on the pull request gate only.
#
# They are NOT suppressed anywhere it matters:
#   - the release workflow scans without a gate, so the SARIF still carries them
#   - the nightly re-scan still opens and updates the tracking issue
#
# Every line expires. When it does, the gate blocks again and somebody has to
# look at whether Cloudflare has shipped a fix — which is the point.

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh v0.53.0 -> fixed in 0.55.0
CVE-2026-56854 exp:2026-10-01

